Cell["XMLMatchQ::badpat: The pattern should be an XMLPattern, an XMLElement pattern, an XMLDocument pattern, a list pattern for a list of elements, or a CSS selector string for one element, or alternatives of these, any of them named, with a condition pat /; test or a test pat?f. A rule gives a value, not a test. A CSS selector such as \"nav a\" or \"ul > li\" depends on what is above the element, which a lone element does not have; use XMLCases or XMLPosition to search a tree with it. Got \"nav a\".", "Message", "MSG"],

